# name: MEOS_ReachabilityFilter
# description: The reachability walk of MEOS over the session of each aircraft, as the walk of the flights of chapter 9 runs it: reachabilityFilterAgg(pos, 100.0) over SESSION(ts, GAP 30 sec), the reports being points of SRID 3857 along the x axis, one per second, and the maximum speed 100 m/s. Aircraft 1 flies two sessions. In the first, of 13 reports from 0 s to 12 s, the first report is 5 km off the track and the twelfth a teleport; the seed is the second report, the first is walked backwards and dropped, the teleport is dropped, so 11 reports are kept. The second session, from 100 s to 102 s, 49.9 km away, is walked on its own and keeps its 3 reports. Aircraft 2, at 0, 1000, 10, 2000 and 20 m from 0 s to 4 s, has 4 of its 5 reports unreachable from the report before, more than half, and is dropped whole. The rows of the two aircraft arrive out of time order. The answers are libmeos's answers for the reports of each session in time order: temporal_reachability_filter_transfn, then temporal_reachability_filter_finalfn.
# groups: [Aggregation, MEOS, SpatioTemporal, WindowOperators]
CREATE LOGICAL SOURCE reports(id UINT64, pos TGEOMPOINT, ts UINT64);
CREATE PHYSICAL SOURCE FOR reports TYPE File SET('|' AS PARSER.FIELD_DELIMITER);
ATTACH INLINE
